WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.850
In 1984, Britain sold shares
in its state telephone

2
00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.600
company to the public.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.910
Gas, water, electricity and rail
followed over the next thirteen years.

4
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.790
Yet in 2002, the rail
track passed to a new body,

5
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.010
Network Rail, now in the public sector.

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.930
So should a country's trains,

7
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.020
water pipes and power
lines be run by the state,

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.000
or by private companies?

9
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.960
In this mission, you'll weigh the
case for and against privatisation,

10
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.590
nationalisation and regulation.

11
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.060
Then you'll lift a cap on
taxi licences in a graph lab,

12
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.440
and predict what happens to fares.

13
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.880
Your mission: find out what
decides whether these industries

14
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.530
serve their customers well.
